  obvious given it's not about from the  satellites but it's from the people  there from the eyewitnesses i think that  the osce monitoring mission also made  this in the in today's report as far as  as far as i was  informed so this is a fact of life  whether it's aggression or not difficult  to say but when you have 120 000 troops  in full uh in full uh capacity to strike  at the border  the line of contact actually i think you  have to be preoccupied and you have to  think about aggression it's not russian  troops on russian territory all right  well look we can trade numbers but one  thing that we are absolutely certain  about is that mr putin has uh  said  that he is going to conduct  nuclear drills and he will oversee them  himself isn't that a rather dangerous  escalation of the situation which you  yourself have just been describing as a  tense one i don't think that everybody  should tell us when we should or  shouldn't conduct drills our drills  happened before we announced a number of  drills beforehand by the way these were  these in bella russia uh that also went  uh in the center of attention were  announced months ago and they are now  being presented as a kind of russian  alleged escalation this is not true i'm  not i'm not i don't think that our  drills on our territory should should  worry anyone yes but mr putin is a smart  man he must know that in the context  announcing a nuclear drill nuclear drill  isn't going to reduce the tensions is it  well if you have nuclear weapons of  course you need to keep keep keep it in  good shape so drills are necessary from  time to time i'm not responsible for  this the question of course i can't  speak for my president in this regard  i'm sure that he had good reasons to  announce these drills uh there are a lot  of issues i think that the world should  be preoccupied more than our drills on  our territory uh so i'm really very much  not understanding uh what is the what is  the point of being super preoccupied  there some western commentators are  saying that  what is actually happening is that mr  putin didn't anticipate  the western resolve that he would have  to face in the form of nato and european  unity  given the buildup of troops on the  ukraine border has he misjudged the  situation i would say that there are a  lot of things for the world to be  preoccupied  right now  and  you shouldn't judge it in terms of chess  board in terms in terms of geopolitical  struggle i think we made quite clear  that we have absolutely legitimate  concerns  about our security  which is being affected by nato  placement of infrastructure and troops  near our border and we we have the right  to be concerned so we made concrete  proposals these proposals are long  overdue it's not the first time that we  voice our preoccupations i think we did  it for tens of years already we base our  preoccupations on the  uh provisions of basic osce documents of  russian nato act and also on some  promises which  western leaders have given us so this is  quite logical and i think what people  what peace loving people in europe  should be preoccupied is really to stop  the militaristic  tune that is now in the heads of many  many western politicians unfortunately  and to to get to negotiating table and  to see what we can together do in terms  of security for guaranteeing uh russia's  absolutely legitimate concerns well can  i just put lastly another reading of  this situation to you which is this  that  mr putin  is rather enjoying this  that he has western leaders coming to  his table he has a western media talking  about him as we are doing now  and that actually the eyes of the world  are on this situation and indeed the  eyes of the russian people are on this  situation diverting them from russia's  own economic problems i think that  enjoying is not the right word that you  can use in these circumstances when we  see absolutely lack of responsibility  from on behalf of western leaders right  now  and a lot of uh scare monitoring and  warm wandering so i don't know anybody  who is enjoying this situation in russia  and what you said about russia's  economic difficulties well every country  has economic difficulties i assume uk  also has some after the brexit  as well there is a trend  that people say that the problems are  narrowed down to ukraine and to solving  this artificial crisis around ukraine  with alleged russian uh in russian plans  to attack but i want to tell you that  the picture is much bigger and ukraine  is only one piece of this puzzle and  that was exactly we assume i assume  personally that it was exactly the  tactics of our western partners to to  start all this hype when we uh  inform them about our proposal and when  we sent to them draft treaties with u.s  and nato about european security this is  a very strange coincidence isn't it  ambassador thank you very much indeed  for your time this morning thank you
 

